  "body": "### What is the issue with the Infra Standard?\n\n[The Notifications spec tries to consume only the initial part of a list](https://notifications.spec.whatwg.org/#create-a-notification-with-a-settings-object):\n\n> 20. For each entry in options[\"[actions](https://notifications.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-notificationoptions-actions)\"], up to the [maximum number of actions](https://notifications.spec.whatwg.org/#maximum-number-of-actions) supported (skip any excess entries):\n\nWould be nice to have an infra term so that it could be something like (the grammar chosen randomly):\n\n> 20. For each entry in the slice(0, 2) of options[\"actions\"]\n\nEdit: 666 😲",
